    "cause_family": "cache_miss",
    "profile": "spring-boot",
    "setup": "Enable the cache but set TTL to 5 seconds. Drive /api/catalog at 50 users for 300 seconds (the full measured window). Most cache entries expire before being reused: the hit ratio is low and the DB sees nearly as many reads as with no cache. The pool fields show moderate pressure; the diagnosis is that cache is configured but not effective.\nNote: this requires perflab.cache.ttl-seconds to be an exposed property. If it is not, use the severe fixture (cache disabled outright) instead.\n",
